This function works by iterating through each character in the input string. If the character is an opening bracket '(', it is pushed onto the stack. If the character is a closing bracket ')', it checks if the stack is empty. If it is, the function returns False because there is no matching opening bracket. If not, it pops the top element from the stack, which represents a matched pair of brackets. Finally, the function checks if the stack is empty, which means all brackets were matched correctly. If it is empty, the function returns True; otherwise, it returns False.

